#---
# purpose: "an ill-typed expression between real side effects is rejected at compile time, so no partial output ever escapes"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: spec/violation
#---
#
# # spec_violation_between_side_effects
#
# `dbg(1)` would print before `:bad + 1` faulted at runtime, and native
# drivers used to swallow that fault after the partial output escaped. The
# Kernel arithmetic `@spec`s reject the middle expression at compile time on
# every path, so neither `1` nor `2` is ever printed and the program never
# runs.
fn main() do
  dbg(1)
  dbg(:bad + 1)
  dbg(2)
end
